<CaseStudy
  title="Hunziker Areal"
  subtitle="Thirteen buildings. A lot of different Tuesdays."
  heroSrc="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/HAL%20014243.jpg?width=1400"
  heroPlaceholder="Hunziker Areal hero — square between the houses (photo needed)"
  heroCredit="Haller Juliet · CC BY-SA 4.0"
  heroCreditHref="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HAL_014243.jpg"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/vauban/', label: 'Vauban' }}
  next={{ href: '/gleis-21/', label: 'Gleis 21' }}
>
  <section class="case-reading mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p>Hunziker Areal opened in Zürich in 2015 with 13 buildings and about 370 homes. The cooperative mehr als wohnen reports housing for roughly 1,200 people, along with workspaces, shops, restaurants and shared facilities. Its published retrospective discusses the project as an experiment with lessons to carry forward. <a class="source-link" href="https://www.mehralswohnen.ch/fileadmin/downloads/Publikationen/Broschuere_maw_engl_inhalt_def_181004.pdf">[Project source]</a></p>
    <p>Housing options include conventional apartments and arrangements with larger shared domestic areas. The buildings vary, but they sit within one larger cooperative framework. It is a neighborhood-scale project with streets and spaces between buildings—not simply a bigger version of La Borda’s enclosed patio.</p>
    <h2>Variety is more useful than one perfect plan.</h2>
    <p>Households change. A useful mix includes choices for people who want sociability, people who want quiet, families, smaller households and people needing support. A range of floor plans helps only if entry rules, costs and accessible routes make that range genuinely available.</p>
    <p>Read a mature project’s retrospective alongside its opening photographs. Ask what was adjusted after move-in, what participation requires, and how much professional management supports resident initiatives. Copying the architecture is the visible part of a much larger undertaking.</p>
    <aside class="research-note mt-8">Reading lens: project publications document the place and its intended design. They are not independent evaluations of affordability, energy performance or how every resident experiences life there. The questions here are our interpretation.</aside>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
<li>Offer different degrees of shared living, rather than making one lifestyle compulsory.</li>
<li>Budget professional operations and resident participation as complementary forms of work.</li>
<li>Learn from post-occupancy experience before repeating the development model.</li>
</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources"><a href="https://www.mehralswohnen.ch/fileadmin/downloads/Publikationen/Broschuere_maw_engl_inhalt_def_181004.pdf">mehr als wohnen · lessons from 2007–2017 (PDF)</a>. Reviewed October 2026. Approximate counts are identified; population changes over time.</Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
